', NULL, N'Administrative-2.3.7', N'2.3.7', N'Third-Party Personnel Security', N'Third-Party Security', N'The organization enforces security controls for third-party personnel and monitors service provider behavior and compliance.', N'Third-party providers include service bureaus, contractors, and other organizations providing control system operation and maintenance, development, IT services, outsourced applications, and network and security management. The organization explicitly includes personnel security controls in acquisitionrelated contract and agreement documents.

', NULL, N'The organization enforces security controls for third-party personnel and monitors service provider behavior and compliance.

', NULL, N'', NULL, N'<FlowDocument xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"><Paragraph Style="{DynamicResource ParagraphTitleFlowDocument}">Third-Party Personnel Security</Paragraph><Section><Paragraph FontStyle="Normal" FontSize="12">Personnel security procedures document the specific security expectations that each member of the organization''s staff is required to meet. Third party personnel security is that aspect of personnel security that defines control and behavioral expectations for contractors, vendors, and other third party entities.</Paragraph></Section><Paragraph FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="13">Requirement</Paragraph><Section Style="{DynamicResource SectionBackgroundFlowDocument}"><Paragraph FontStyle="Italic" FontSize="12">The organization enforces security controls for third-party personnel and monitors service provider behavior and compliance.</Paragraph></Section><Paragraph FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="13">Supplemental Guidance</Paragraph><Section><Paragraph FontStyle="Normal" FontSize="12">Third-party providers include service bureaus, contractors, and other organizations providing control system operation and maintenance, development, IT services, outsourced applications, and network and security management. The organization explicitly includes personnel security controls in acquisitionrelated contract and agreement documents.</Paragraph></Section><Paragraph FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="13">Requirement Enhancements</Paragraph><Section><Paragraph FontStyle="Normal" FontSize="12">None</Paragraph></Section><Paragraph FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="13">References</Paragraph><Paragraph FontStyle="Normal" FontSize="12">NIST Special Publication 800-53 Revision 3 PS-7</Paragraph><Paragraph FontStyle="Normal" FontSize="12">American Petroleum Institute Pipeline SCADA Security Standard API 1164 2nd Edition 3.1</Paragraph><Paragraph FontStyle="Normal" FontSize="12">North American Electric Reliability Corporation (NERC) CIPS CIP 004-3, A-3