', NULL, N'Administrative-2.3.8', N'2.3.8', N'Personnel Accountability', N'Personnel Account', N'The organization employs a formal accountability process for personnel failing to comply with established control system security policies and procedures and clearly documents potential disciplinary actions for failing to comply.', N'The organization ensures that the accountability process is consistent with applicable federal and local government statutory requirements (directives, policies, and regulations), standards, and guidance. The accountability process can be included as part of the organization’s general personnel policies and procedures.

', NULL, N'The organization employs a formal accountability process for personnel failing to comply with established control system security policies and procedures and clearly documents potential disciplinary actions for failing to comply.

', NULL, N'', NULL, N'<FlowDocument xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"><Paragraph Style="{DynamicResource ParagraphTitleFlowDocument}">Personnel Accountability</Paragraph><Section><Paragraph FontStyle="Normal" FontSize="12">Personnel security procedures document the specific security expectations that each member of the organization''s staff is required to meet. Personnel accountability is that aspect of personnel security that defines how noncompliance will be handled.</Paragraph></Section><Paragraph FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="13">Requirement</Paragraph><Section Style="{DynamicResource SectionBackgroundFlowDocument}"><Paragraph FontStyle="Italic" FontSize="12">The organization employs a formal accountability process for personnel failing to comply with established control system security policies and procedures and clearly documents potential disciplinary actions for failing to comply.</Paragraph></Section><Paragraph FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="13">Supplemental Guidance</Paragraph><Section><Paragraph FontStyle="Normal" FontSize="12">The organization ensures that the accountability process is consistent with applicable federal and local government statutory requirements (directives, policies, and regulations), standards, and guidance. The accountability process can be included as part of the organization’s general personnel policies and procedures.</Paragraph></Section><Paragraph FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="13">Requirement Enhancements</Paragraph><Section><Paragraph FontStyle="Normal" FontSize="12">None</Paragraph></Section><Paragraph FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="13">References</Paragraph><Paragraph FontStyle="Normal" FontSize="12">NIST Special Publication 800-53 Revision 3 PS-8</Paragraph><Paragraph FontStyle="Normal" FontSize="12">American Petroleum Institute Pipeline SCADA Security Standard API 1164 2nd Edition 1.2</Paragraph><Paragraph FontStyle="Normal" FontSize="12">North American Electric Reliability Corporation (NERC) CIPS CIP 