', NULL, N'<FlowDocument xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"><Paragraph Style="{DynamicResource ParagraphTitleFlowDocument}">Emergency Shutoff</Paragraph><Section><Paragraph FontStyle="Normal" FontSize="12">Physical and environmental security encompasses protection of physical assets from damage, misuse, or theft. Emergency shutoff is an aspect of physical and environmental security. It deals with protecting emergency power shutoff capability.</Paragraph></Section><Paragraph FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="13">Requirement</Paragraph><Section Style="{DynamicResource SectionBackgroundFlowDocument}"><Paragraph FontStyle="Italic" FontSize="12">The organization, for specific locations within a facility containing concentrations of control system resources, protects emergency power shutoff capability from unauthorized activation.</Paragraph></Section><Paragraph FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="13">Supplemental Guidance</Paragraph><Section><Paragraph FontStyle="Normal" FontSize="12">The design of the control systems facility includes an emergency shutoff to cut power to critical control system resources outside any area prone to flooding.</Paragraph></Section><Paragraph FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="13">Requirement Enhancements</Paragraph><Section><List MarkerStyle="Decimal"><ListItem><Paragraph FontStyle="Normal" FontSize="12">The organization protects the emergency power-off capability from accidental and intentional/unauthorized activation.</Paragraph></ListItem></List></Section><Paragraph FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="13">References</Paragraph><Paragraph FontStyle="Normal" FontSize="12">NIST Special Publication 800-53 Revision 3 PE-10</Paragraph><Paragraph FontStyle="Normal" FontSize="12">American Petroleum Institute Pipeline SCADA Security Standard API 1164 2nd Edition Annex A</Paragraph><Paragraph FontStyle="Normal" FontSize="12">NRC Cyber Security Programs for Nuclear Facilities Regulatory Guide 5.71 C.3.2, App. C.3.11, App. C.6, App. C.8, App. C.9<