', NULL, N'Administrative-2.4.10', N'2.4.10', N'Emergency Lighting', N'Emergency Lighting', N'The organization employs and maintains automatic emergency lighting systems that activate in the event of a power outage or disruption and includes lighting for emergency exits and evacuation routes.', N'This control may be satisfied by similar requirements fulfilled by another organizational entity other than the control system security program. Organizations should avoid duplicating actions already covered.

', NULL, N'The organization employs and maintains automatic emergency lighting systems that activate in the event of a power outage or disruption and includes lighting for emergency exits and evacuation routes.

', NULL, N'', NULL, N'<FlowDocument xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"><Paragraph Style="{DynamicResource ParagraphTitleFlowDocument}">Emergency Lighting</Paragraph><Section><Paragraph FontStyle="Normal" FontSize="12">Physical and environmental security encompasses protection of physical assets from damage, misuse, or theft. Emergency lighting is an aspect of physical and environmental security. It deals with maintaining an emergency lighting system.</Paragraph></Section><Paragraph FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="13">Requirement</Paragraph><Section Style="{DynamicResource SectionBackgroundFlowDocument}"><Paragraph FontStyle="Italic" FontSize="12">The organization employs and maintains automatic emergency lighting systems that activate in the event of a power outage or disruption and includes lighting for emergency exits and evacuation routes.</Paragraph></Section><Paragraph FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="13">Supplemental Guidance</Paragraph><Section><Paragraph FontStyle="Normal" FontSize="12">This control may be satisfied by similar requirements fulfilled by another organizational entity other than the control system security program. Organizations should avoid duplicating actions already covered.</Paragraph></Section><Paragraph FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="13">Requirement Enhancements</Paragraph><Section><Paragraph FontStyle="Normal" FontSize="12">None</Paragraph></Section><Paragraph FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="13">References</Paragraph><Paragraph FontStyle="Normal" FontSize="12">NIST Special Publication 800-53 Revision 3 PE-12</Paragraph><Paragraph FontStyle="Normal" FontSize="12">American Petroleum Institute Pipeline SCADA Security Standard API 1164 2nd Edition 4, Annex A</Paragraph><Paragraph FontStyle="Normal" FontSize="12">NRC Cyber Security Programs for Nuclear Facilities Regulatory Guide 5.71 C.3.2, App. C.9</Paragraph></FlowDocument>')
', NULL, N'Administrative-2.4.11', N'2.4.11', N'Fire Protection', N'Fire Protection', N'The organization implements and maintains fire suppression and detection devices/systems that can be activated in the event of a fire.
Requirement Enhancement 1 - The organization employs fire detection devices/systems that activate automatically and notify the organization and emergency responders in the event of a fire.
Requirement Enhancement 2 - The organization employs fire suppression devices/systems that provide automatic notification of any activation to the organization and emergency responders.
Requirement Enhancement 3 - The organization employs an automatic fire suppression capability in facilities that are not staffed continuously.', N'Fire suppression and detection devices/systems include sprinkler systems, handheld fire extinguishers, fixed fire hoses, and smoke detectors. This control may be satisfied by similar requirements fulfilled by another organizational entity other than the control system security program. Organizations should avoid duplicating actions already covered.

