outstanding', N'Issue prepaid cards internally, through a third party, or on behalf of other financial institutions; >20,000 cards outstanding', N'If a prepaid card program existsDiscuss with management the volume of prepaid cards issued directly or via a third party service provider.', 20, N'Prepaid cards', N'There are several types of prepaid cards, including gift, payroll and travel cards. The issuance of prepaid cards subject financial institutions to legal risks. For example, prepaid card product programs must comply with the Bank Secrecy Act and anti-money laundering guidance. Prepaid cards issued by the financial institution may be distributed and marketed by a third-party; however, the complexity can increase to direct issuance  of the cards or issuing the cards on behalf of other financial institutions. Prepaid access cards can be used to perpetrate money laundering schemes in addition to other risks such as account take over, package/gift card tampering, card altering, conversion and bulk cash smuggling, and trade-based money laundering.', N'IRP')
