>100,000 merchants', N'If the credit union provides merchant processing, discus with management the number of merchants for whom they provide this service.', 20, N'Merchant acquirer (sponsor merchants or card processor activity into the payment system)', N'To accept credit card payments, merchants must be sponsored by an acquiring institution that is a member of the credit card association. A merchant acquirer contracts directly with merchants or indirectly through an agent institution or third-party to provide card processing. Acquiring institutions typically provide all backroom operations and own the Bank Identification Number (BIN)/Interbank Card Association (ICA) settlement number. Do not include institutions acting as referring agents only, regardless of whether they have accepted liability for merchant transactions.', N'IRP')
