phishing campaigns targeting high net worth customers and employees at the institution or third parties supporting critical activities; Institution specifically is named in threat reports; may ha', N'Substantial number of attempts monthly (>100,000); persistent attempts to attack senior management and/or network administrators; frequently targeted for DDoS attacks', N'Review the report to the board on the annual compliance with the ISP, the IT steering or other management committee, the incident reports for security events occurring since the last exam.  Discuss with management the number of security events or cyber attacks attempted since the last examination.', 43, N'Attempted cyber attacks', N'Attempted cyber attacks, whether successful or not, should be logged and tracked to establish and understand normal volume baseline in order to detect attacks and anomolous activity. Examples of cyber attacks include:
• Generic phishing: an attempt to acquire sensitive information through electronic communication (typically email or mimicked websites) by acting as a trustworthy entity.
• Spear phishing: similar goals as generic phishing; however, it is (targeted at specific individuals, companies, and/or third-parties). With spear phishing the attacker may increase their success rate through reconnaissance on the target.
• DDoS (distributed denial of service) attacks: when multiple systems [operated by or for the benefit of the attacker(s)] flood the bandwidth or resources of the targeted system (usually one or more webservers operated by the financial institution).', N'IRP')
