<ul>
<li>Web browsers represent a common point of entry for malicious attack. Leverage email and web browser security settings to protect against spoofed or modified emails and unsecured webpages. Content filtering applied to external websites can prevent attackers from delivering malicious code to desktop applications. Firewalls can also deny traffic to potentially harmful sites while allowing access to acceptable applications.</li>
<li>Updating the browsers security settings can make it much harder for malware to get installed. As an example, settings can be employed to reduce the ability of installing plugins and other add-ons and to disable certain types of content from automatically executing.</li>
