Critical section leadership, Physical & Cybersecurity Personnel, Third Party Contractors, Vendors, & Suppliers', N'<p>All roles and responsibilities involving cybersecurity should be documented in an organization’s cybersecurity policy, to include a single authoritative position responsible for the overall cybersecurity program.</p><p>Roles and responsibilities related to the cybersecurity policy and program are distributed across the organization. Third-party contractors can also be involved to assist with these activities.</p><p>Ensure that legal and regulatory requirements regarding cybersecurity, including privacy, are implemented and managed.</p><p>Collaboration between Information Technology (IT) and Operational Technology (OT) is recommended to streamline processes, enhance security measures, and boost operational effectiveness.</p>', N'Lack of sufficient cybersecurity accountability, investment, or effectiveness.', N'<div><a href="https://www.cisa.gov/sites/default/files/publications/Focus_Areas_for_CEOs.pdf" target="_blank">Shields Up: 5 Urgent Cybersecurity Actions for Executives</a></div><div><a href="https://niccs.cisa.gov/workforce-development/nice-framework/work-role/executive-cybersecurity-leadership" target="_blank">Executive Cybersecurity Leadership</a></div>', N'Roles, responsibilities, and authorities related to the organization''s cybersecurity program are established, communicated, understood, enforced, and aligned within the organization and external partners.', N'Establish Cybersecurity Responsibilities', N'<p class="fst-italic">All bullets for an answer option must be satisfied to meet the criteria for that answer.</p>  <div class="sub-header-2">OT - Implemented</div>  <ul>  <li>Does the organization have a designated name, role/position/title that is responsible for planning resourcing and executing OT activities?</li>  </ul>  <div class="sub-header-2">IT - Implemented</div>  <ul>  <li>Does the organization have a designated individual identified as responsible and accountable for planning, resourcing, and execution of cybersecurity activities?  (e.g., a CISO)</li>  <li>Is the control in place, such that any remaining gaps are relatively minor?  (< 3% gaps)</li>  </ul>  <div class="sub-header-2">In Progress</div>  <ul>  <li>Is the organization actively working to implement this control, such that it is at least 10% implemented?</li>  </ul>  <div class="sub-header-2">Scoped</div>  <ul>  <li>Does the organization have a plan and funding allocated to implement this goal?  (i.e., at least a POA&M with allocated funding for it?)</li>  </ul>  <div class="sub-header-2">Not Implemented</div>  <ul>  <li>None of the above implementation levels are met.</li>  </ul>  ')
<div class="sub-header-2">OT - Implemented</div>
<ul>
<li>For OT assets where patching is either not possible or may substantially compromise availability or safety, are compensating controls applied and recorded, such that the ability of threat actors to exploit the vulnerabilities is reduced?</li>
<li>The organization provides additional consideration for organizations including testing and validation to ensure that the patches do not impact operational capabilities or safety.</li>
</ul>
<div class="sub-header-2">IT - Implemented</div>
<ul>
<li>Does the organization regularly review, update, communicate, and enforce the policies for managing the cybersecurity program?</li>
<li>Is the control in place, such that any remaining gaps are relatively minor?  (< 3% gaps)</li>
</ul>
