    <p class=''p1''>ICT supply chain concerns of contingency planning include planning for alternative suppliers of system components, alternative suppliers of systems and services, denial of service attacks to the supply chain, and planning for alternate delivery routes for critical system components. Additionally, many techniques used for contingency planning, such as alternative processing sites, have their own ICT supply chains including their own specific ICT supply chain risks. Organizations should ensure that they understand and manage ICT supply chain risks and dependencies related to the contingency planning activities as necessary.</p>
